<div class="rest-connection">
  <div class="rest-connection-fields">
    <label>
      Endpoint
      <input
        id="rest-endpoint"
        type="url"
        placeholder="https://your-cluster.example.com"
        autocomplete="off"
      />
    </label>
    <label>
      Bearer token (optional)
      <input
        id="rest-token"
        type="password"
        autocomplete="off"
        spellcheck="false"
      />
    </label>
    <label>
      Collection
      <select id="rest-collection" disabled>
        <option value="">Run List collections</option>
      </select>
    </label>
  </div>
  <details>
    <summary>Connection and CORS help</summary>
    <p>
      Use HTTPS for remote clusters or HTTP on loopback. Requests go directly
      from your browser to the endpoint. When copying an authenticated cURL
      command, set <code>MILVUS_TOKEN</code> in your shell.
    </p>
    <p>
      For cross-origin requests, configure the endpoint to answer OPTIONS and
      allow the docs origin, POST, Content-Type, and Authorization if you use a
      token. Try the copied cURL command to troubleshoot outside the browser.
    </p>
  </details>
  <p role="status" id="rest-selection-status"></p>
</div>
